<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Wapinitia and Salmon River Overlooks (from Snow Bunny Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:150-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.287270" lon="-121.728448"><ele>1169.1</ele><name>Snow Bunny Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:snow-bunny-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019327), north side of US 26; confidence: high; pdf_page: 152; quote: the 5.8-mile one-way ski tour from Snow Bunny</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286395" lon="-121.728058"><ele>1160.2</ele><name>Trillium Lake Road at US 26</name><desc>source: OSM node 37465886, start of Trillium Lake Road NF 2656 (the book's Snow Bunny Hill road) across the highway; confidence: high; pdf_page: 142</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Road and Trillium Lake Loop Road (NF 2656), node 37397443, east of the lake by the campground; confidence: high; pdf_page: 146; quote: From the campground junction east of Trillium Lake (see map) take the road angling uphill for a long, gentle climb to the Jefferson Viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247437" lon="-121.738521"><ele>1193.3</ele><name>Jefferson Viewpoint</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 37598739, 1.79 mi from the campground junction (osm_lookup along), at the road's sweeping turn east; DEM 3,915 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 146; book_elev_ft: 3940; quote: 1.8 miles from the junction and 3.5 miles from the sno-park ... The road makes a sweeping turn at the viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.243053" lon="-121.733122"><ele>1211.2</ele><name>High Divide (Lostman Trail junction)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Trillium Lake Loop Road and Lost Man Trail, node 2452534627; DEM 3,974 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; book_elev_ft: 4040; quote: Follow the Mud Creek Ridge road 0.6 mile beyond the Jefferson Viewpoint to the High Divide ... Here, the Lostman Trail is the obvious side road to the left (east).</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.229466" lon="-121.744614"><ele>1133.2</ele><name>Big Bend</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 2452545085, the loop's southern tip where the High Divide road turns north as the Lower Ridge road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 147</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.231206" lon="-121.748168"><ele>1121.3</ele><name>Side road west (on Loop Road)</name><desc>source: OSM Trillium Lake Loop Road node 37598919, nearest to the east end of unnamed OSM track way/238032538 (15 m gap); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150; quote: Just west of Big Bend look for a side road to the west along the bottom of a clearcut. This road leads to Asgard Meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.231150" lon="-121.748360"><ele>1121.0</ele><name>Side road start</name><desc>source: OSM node 2459019637, east end of track way/238032538; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.228600" lon="-121.762790"><ele>1088.2</ele><name>Past Asgard Meadow</name><desc>source: OSM track way/238032538 node 2452545241, past the curve where track 237337444 (the Highline Cutoff side road) leaves north at node 2452545242; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 152; quote: continue around the curve and ski past Asgard Meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.227900" lon="-121.763100"><ele>1112.9</ele><name>Wapinitia Overlook knoll</name><desc>source: DEM local high point (3,651 ft) about 300 yd past the curve, its south side dropping 250 ft to the Salmon River; map 33 star just south of Asgard Mdw; confidence: low; pdf_page: 152; quote: 300 yards farther across a large, nearly level clearcut to an obvious knoll. Climb the knoll for views here at the Wapinitia Overlook.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Wapinitia and Salmon River Overlooks (from Snow Bunny Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Snow Bunny Sno-Park -&gt; Trillium Lake Road at US 26: straight (high), 0.06 mi | 2. Trillium Lake Road at US 26 -&gt; Campground junction: osm (high), 1.38 mi | 3. Campground junction -&gt; Jefferson Viewpoint: osm (high), 1.79 mi | 4. Jefferson Viewpoint -&gt; High Divide (Lostman Trail junction): osm (high), 0.55 mi | 5. High Divide (Lostman Trail junction) -&gt; Big Bend: osm (high), 1.13 mi | 6. Big Bend -&gt; Side road west (on Loop Road): osm (high), 0.25 mi | 7. Side road west (on Loop Road) -&gt; Side road start: straight (medium), 0.01 mi | 8. Side road start -&gt; Past Asgard Meadow: osm (medium), 0.77 mi | 9. Past Asgard Meadow -&gt; Wapinitia Overlook knoll: straight (low), 0.05 mi</desc>
